1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:05,546
Ten minutes a day beats a weekend of
nothing. It sounds too small to work.

2
00:00:07,096 --> 00:00:10,863
The number is ten. Ten minutes, every day.

3
00:00:12,413 --> 00:00:18,488
One weekend marathon. Or ten minutes
daily, for a month. Same hours.

4
00:00:20,038 --> 00:00:22,542
Pick one skill. Set a timer.

5
00:00:23,512 --> 00:00:27,407
And stop when it rings, even if you are
enjoying it.

6
00:00:28,957 --> 00:00:34,467
Fifty percent practice. Twenty percent
notes. Thirty percent sleep.

7
00:00:35,437 --> 00:00:36,867
Sleep is the practice.

8
00:00:38,417 --> 00:00:43,201
One rep, one note, one night. That is the
whole stack.

9
00:00:44,751 --> 00:00:50,558
Same hours. A skill in a year, or a skill
in a month. One you keep.

10
00:00:52,108 --> 00:00:55,233
Ten minutes, one skill, every day.

11
00:00:56,783 --> 00:01:00,131
Start the timer today. Ten minutes is
enough.
